WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.467
Not every transformation makes the same kind of claim.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:12.872
If an email contains extra spaces and uppercase letters, trimming it and converting it to lowercase usually changes only

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:16.752
the representation. We still believe it refers to the same email address.

00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:24.562
If a business rule says the labels tech, electronic, and electronics all represent one category,

00:00:24.562 --> 00:00:29.391
mapping them to Electronics is also a documented standardization.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:35.742
But changing a negative price of negative fifty to positive fifty is different.

00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:39.197
Now we are claiming that we know the true price.

00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:41.332
That requires evidence.

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:49.182
A useful question is: am I changing how the same information is represented, or am I claiming that the underlying fact

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:53.852
itself is different? Standardize when equivalence is known.

00:00:53.852 --> 00:00:59.649
Correct a fact only when the correct value is supported by a trustworthy source or rule.
